// Specialised: research.

:: anchor=left size=20 pad=26 enter=type speed=44 line=1.4

@Signals Officer
:: point=tab.research gate=1 until=open:research
Research. Open it -- the complaint is always the same -- nothing you start ever seems to
finish -- and it is not a bug, it is the point.
---
@Signals Officer
Everything here is measured in turns you have not played yet. A thing you
start now lands long after you have forgotten wanting it, which means the only
bad time to start is later.
---
@Signals Officer
It draws from the same money the army does. A country that researches
everything fields nothing, and a country that fields everything is still
fighting last decade's war in twenty turns' time.

Pick a lane. Do not pick all of them.
---
@Signals Officer
:: point=panel.close gate=1 until=closed:research
Close it again -- the §**x**§ in the corner.
---
@Signals Officer
Finished work does not apply itself retroactively. New equipment reaches new
formations first, so the turn something completes is the turn to look at what
you are building, not the turn to relax.

That is research. Anything else?
